OL,3,AHousehold energy bills to hit
OL,4,Athree-year high as Ofgem announces 4%
OL,5,Arise from October
OL,6,
OL,7,FEnergy prices for millions of
OL,8,Fhouseholds will rise to the highest
OL,9,Flevel for three years, under regulator
OL,10,FOfgem's price cap.
OL,12,FOfgem said the price cap will increase
OL,13,Fby 4% on 1 October, driven by higher
OL,14,Fwholesale gas prices due to the Iran
OL,15,Fwar.
OL,17,FA household using a typical amount of
OL,18,Fgas and electricity will pay #60 a year
OL,19,Fmore, but more than a third of
OL,20,Fhouseholds are on fixed tariffs so
OL,21,Ftheir prices will not change.
OL,23,APub: 25-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB  BusinessC Nat TVF  Nat News
